    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is just the acceptance tests (the other two files are a base class and a helper). All tests pass with a clean `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `contactPreference` derived field so the API returns `EMAIL` when an owner has an email, otherwise `PHONE`.\n\nTwo changes, matching the existing pattern for derived fields (`membershipLevel`, `locality`, etc.):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema (the OpenAPI generator produces the `OwnerDto` field at build time).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` that derives the value from the owner's own field:\n   ```java\n   (owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank()) ? \"EMAIL\" : \"PHONE\"\n   ```\n\nThis treats email presence consistently with the existing `membershipLevel` logic (non-null and non-blank). Both acceptance tests (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) and the full suite pass: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
